Immediate needs
---------------
rrclient: Need to split gtk into its own package as a loadable module using events asap

* Move all socket code out of librrprotocol
  - It needs to go into client and server code
    - client glib/wslay
    - server glib/wslay OR libmongoose

* Elmer/noob mode needs a dialog confirmation system
  - Noob requests elevated privs and is cautioned about their responsibility
  - Elmers are prompted and one can accept responsibility for the user

* Support for multiple rigs

* Anywhere with a bool return type needs to ensure
  that it returns true on success, false on failure
  - currently some places, we still use 0 for success, which is incorrect
    - these should be *mostly* gone but need fixed immediately if found!

codec negotiation: Discard codecs without configured pipelines from the list?

rrclient: Consider bringing in sqlite db for storage/caching (call lookups, etc)

*: Rotator/amp/ATU support
   - backend.internal, backend.hamlib, and backend.network based

librustyaxe: logger - extend log.level so its work like log.level=*:info,event:crazy@10,6 to allow 10 messages in 6 seconds. Would that be too much work?

rrclient/rrserver: Maybe support storing config in the db too? So load config file then apply db? Would need to periodically poll db for changes tho, ugly..

* WebTransport support
  - https://github.com/ngtcp2/ngtcp2/
  - https://github.com/ngtcp2/nghttp3/
  - https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebTransport#examples
